        "content": [
          "\\begin{theorem}\\label{three:thm:regular-four}\nFix a positive density bound $\\alpha$ and ordinary robust parameters\nwith sufficiently small range. For sufficiently small $\\eps>0$\nand large even $n$, let $R$ be a simple $k$-regular graph of order\n$n$ with no $k$-overfull set, where $k\\ge\\alpha n$ and\n\\[\n V(R)=U_1\\cup\\cdots\\cup U_q\\cup Z,\\qquad q\\in\\{3,4\\},\n \\qquad |U_i|\\ge\\alpha n.\n\\]\nIf the $U_i$ contain cores of error $a$ and\n$a+|Z|+1\\le\\eps n$, then $R$ has a $1$-factorization.\n\\end{theorem}"
